<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011T">Proposition <span data-tag="011T">3.4.4.3</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \overline{C} \ar [d] &amp;  \overline{A} \ar [l] \ar [r]^-{\overline{i}} \ar [d] &amp;  \overline{B} \ar [d] \\ C &amp;  A \ar [r]^-{i} \ar [l] &amp;  B, } \]
</div>
<p> in which both squares are homotopy pullbacks. If $i$ and $\overline{i}$ are monomorphisms, then both squares in the induced diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \overline{C} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \overline{C} \coprod _{ \overline{A} } \overline{B} \ar [d] &amp;  \overline{B} \ar [l] \ar [d] \\ C \ar [r] &amp;  C \coprod _{ A} B &amp;  B \ar [l] } \]
</div>
<p> are also also homotopy pullbacks. </p>
</article>
